package.json: "@codedev/grading-client": "^2.4.0"   (published only on npm.codedev.test, latest 2.6.1)

.npmrc in the repository:
registry=https://registry.npmjs.org/
//npm.codedev.test/:_authToken=${CODEDEV_NPM_TOKEN}

~/.npmrc on every developer laptop:
@codedev:registry=https://npm.codedev.test/

CI log (npm install):
npm http fetch GET 200 https://registry.npmjs.org/@codedev%2fgrading-client 212ms
added 1 package: @codedev/grading-client@2.99.0

Statement: "Adding @codedev:registry=https://npm.codedev.test/ to the repository's .npmrc makes npm request every @codedev/* package from npm.codedev.test only, so this project can no longer install the public 2.99.0."
